H.2 Escalation Protocol: Human–AI Disagreement

```
WHEN AI_confidence(task) < threshold_high AND AI_confidence(task) > threshold_low:
    IF human_recommendation EXISTS AND human_recommendation != AI_recommendation:
        ESCALATE to Level 1 Reviewer
        
        Level 1 Review (HATA or designated supervisor):
        - Review AI reasoning trace
        - Review human rationale
        - IF time_to_decision < d(t)*0.3: make final call
        - ELSE: escalate to Level 2
        
        Level 2 Review (domain expert panel, n>=3):
        - Blind vote (AI vs human recommendation)
        - Majority binds
        - Log decision for training
        
    ELSE IF human_recommendation DOES NOT EXIST:
        Default to AI_recommendation with logging
        
WHEN AI_confidence(task) >= threshold_high:
    Execute AI_recommendation automatically (if H(t)=0)
    
WHEN AI_confidence(task) <= threshold_low:
    Default to human execution or supervised AI
```

Default thresholds: $\text{threshold\_high} = 0.95$, $\text{threshold\_low} = 0.70$

